cast_shell: advertise VP9 in the stub media capabilities

CastContentRendererClient::IsDecoderSupportedVideoType asks
MediaCapabilitiesShlib::IsSupportedVideoConfig on every non-Android build,
and that symbol resolves into libcast_media_1.0.so. With no vendor backend
the shlib is cast_media_dummy.cc, which claims H.264 and VP8 only - so
MediaSource.isTypeSupported rejects VP9 and players that offer nothing else
fall back to a generic error.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on board-specific decoder set]

Signed-off-by: Joey Eamigh <55670930+JoeyEamigh@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/chromecast/media/cma/backend/cast_media_dummy.cc
+++ b/chromecast/media/cma/backend/cast_media_dummy.cc
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
 bool MediaCapabilitiesShlib::IsSupportedVideoConfig(VideoCodec codec,
                                                     VideoProfile profile,
                                                     int level) {
-  return (codec == kCodecH264 || codec == kCodecVP8);
+  return (codec == kCodecH264 || codec == kCodecVP8 || codec == kCodecVP9);
 }
 
 bool MediaCapabilitiesShlib::IsSupportedAudioConfig(const AudioConfig& config) {
